generated_questions.scenario_preamble:
Consider a particle of mass $m$ in a 1D infinite square well of width $L$:

$$V(x)=\begin{cases}
0, & 0\le x\le L\\
\infty, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}$$

Inside the well the energy is $E>0$ and you may define $k^2=\frac{2mE}{\hbar^2}$.
